    instagramCaption:
      "Most women spend more time researching strollers than preparing their body for birth.\n\nAnd honestly?\n\nI don\u2019t blame them.\n\nWe\u2019re told what supplements to take.\nWhat foods to avoid.\nWhat week the baby is the size of a mango.\n\nBut very few women are taught how to physically prepare for labour.\n\nAs a Women\u2019s Health Physiotherapist, that\u2019s the gap I see every day.\n\nBecause birth isn\u2019t only about the baby.\n\nIt\u2019s also about the person giving birth.\n\nYour strength.\nYour endurance.\nYour confidence.\nYour ability to move, adapt, breathe, and recover.\n\nThat\u2019s why research around pregnancy exercise and prenatal Pilates excites me.\n\nNot because one exercise is \u201Cbetter\u201D than another.\n\nBut because we\u2019re finally talking about preparing for birth.. not just surviving pregnancy.\n\nMy hope is that future moms stop asking:\n\n\u201CIs it safe to exercise during pregnancy?\u201D\n\nAnd start asking:\n\n\u201CHow can I use exercise to support my pregnancy, labour, pelvic floor health, and postpartum recovery?\u201D\n\nThat\u2019s a much more powerful conversation \u{1F90D}\n\n\u{1F4AC} If you\u2019re pregnant, what\u2019s one thing nobody told you about preparing for birth?\n\n\u{1F447}\u{1F3FD} Let\u2019s talk about it.\n\n\u{1F4CC} Save this for your pregnancy journey.\n\u{1F90D} Share with a mom-to-be who\u2019d appreciate this perspective.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n#prenatal #pilates #pregnancyexercise #laboranddelivery #explore",
