    instagramCaption:
      "\u201CYour periods are irregular?\nHere, take these pills.\u201D\n\nFor YEARS, that was the reality for so many girls with PCOS \u{1F440}\n\nNo one spoke enough about:\nthe exhaustion, the acne, the rapid weight changes, the cravings, the hair fall, the anxiety, the frustration of feeling like your body was working against you.\n\nAnd one of the biggest problems?\nThe name itself.\n\nPolycystic Ovary Syndrome made it sound like this condition was ONLY about ovaries & cysts\u2026 while so many women were struggling with symptoms affecting their entire body.\n\nWhich is why PCOS is now officially being called:\n\n\u2728 PMOS - Polyendocrine Metabolic Ovarian Syndrome \u2728\n\nA name that finally acknowledges:\n\u25AB\uFE0F hormones\n\u25AB\uFE0F metabolism\n\u25AB\uFE0F insulin resistance\n\u25AB\uFE0F fertility\n\u25AB\uFE0F mental health\n\u25AB\uFE0F long-term health\n\n..not just PERIODS.\n\nAnd honestly?\nFor many girls, this feels validating.\n\nBecause maybe you were never \u201Coverreacting.\u201D\nMaybe your symptoms were simply being overlooked all along \u{1F90D}\n\n\u{1F4CC} Save this post \n\u{1F4E4} Share it with someone who has PMOS/PCOS\n\u{1F4AC} And tell us honestly in the comments..\nWere you also just given pills to regulate your cycles while the bigger picture was ignored?\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ pcos, pmos, pcod, irregular periods, insulin resistance, endocrinology, metabolic disorder, polyendocrine metabolic ovarian syndrome, girls with pcos, relatable, hormonal imbalance, facial hair, androgens, physical activity, diet and nutrition, diabetes, pmos is the new pcos, new name of pcos, womens health, gynecologist, women\u2019s heath physiotherapist, explore page, trending]\n#pmos #pcos #newname #polyendocrinemetabolicovariansyndrome #fyp",
