    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "You\u2019re taking your prenatal supplements\u2026 but are they actually getting absorbed? \u{1F930}\u{1F3FB}\u{1F48A}\u{1F440}\n\nPregnancy nutrition isn\u2019t just about what goes in.. \nit\u2019s about what actually gets absorbed, utilised, and reaches your baby.\n\nAnd physiologically, a lot is happening behind the scenes \u2B07\uFE0F\n\n\u2192 Your gut absorption isn\u2019t constant during pregnancy\nHormonal shifts (hello progesterone) slow gastric motility \u2192\nnutrients sit longer, absorption becomes inconsistent, bloating increases\nSo some days you feel great\u2026 some days, not so much\n\n\u2192 Minerals share the same transport pathways\nInside your intestine, nutrients like iron, calcium, zinc use overlapping carriers\n\u2192 If they arrive together, they literally compete at a cellular level\nResult? Lower net absorption despite \u201Ctaking everything\u201D\n\n\u2192 Your body prioritises the baby first\nEven with borderline intake, fetal requirements are maintained\n\u2192 Which means you may feel the fatigue, weakness, cramps first\n\n\u2192 Muscle + tissue demand increases silently\nAs your body adapts (posture changes, weight shifts),\nyour nutritional needs aren\u2019t just for baby but also for your musculoskeletal system\n\u2192 This is why some women feel unexpected aches, low strength, slower recovery\n\nSo if you\u2019ve been thinking,\n\u201CI\u2019m eating well, taking supplements\u2026 why do I still feel this way?\u201D\nthere\u2019s a real physiological reason behind it.\n\nLet\u2019s make pregnancy feel better, not just look \u201Cnormal\u201D on reports.\n\n\u2728 Save this.. because timing, combinations & balance matter more than you think \u2714\uFE0F\nShare this with a mom-to-be who\u2019s trying her best but still feels confused \u{1F90D}\n\n\u{1F4E9} Comment \u201CPRENATAL\u201D for a personalised, evidence-based plan\n\u2192 tailored to your body, your trimester, your symptoms!\u{1FAF6}\u{1F3FB}\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ pregnancy supplements, prenatal supplements, supplement timing, iron, calcium, folate, folic acid, protein intake during pregnancy, importance of supplements in pregnancy, what supplements to take during pregnancy, what helps iron absorption better, fetal development, baby growth, what helps with baby\u2019s growth, pregnancy, diet and nutrition, gynecologist, women\u2019s health physiotherapist, womenshealthduo ]\n#prenatal #supplements #pregnancydiet #pregnancynutrition #fyp",
