    topics: ["Exercise", "Menstrual health", "Carousel"],
    title:
      "\u{1F538}When it comes to PCOS, people often focus on weight gain and irregular periods, but the reality is far more complex!",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u{1F538}When it comes to PCOS, people often focus on weight gain and irregular periods, but the reality is far more complex!\n\u{1F538}PCOS isn\u2019t just about reproductive symptoms; it\u2019s a full-body condition that can impact everything from your skin to your mental health.\n\n\u27A1\uFE0F Beyond the common symptoms, many people with PCOS experience things like:\n\n\u25AA\uFE0FFatigue that makes daily tasks feel extra challenging \n\u25AA\uFE0FBrain fog and difficulty concentrating \n\u25AA\uFE0FAcanthosis nigricans: dark, velvety skin patches, often around the neck or underarms \n\u25AA\uFE0FHirsutism (excess hair growth) on the face, chest, or back \n\u25AA\uFE0FAlopecia (hair thinning) on the scalp \n\u25AA\uFE0FMood swings and higher levels of anxiety or depression due to hormonal shifts\n& much more\n\n\u{1F538}PCOS can also bring on low-grade inflammation and insulin resistance, which can increase the risk of diabetes and heart disease over time!\n\n\u2728Taking a holistic approach can make a real difference in managing these diverse symptoms. \n\u{1F469}\u{1F3FB}\u200D\u2695\uFE0FConsulting with your gynecologist, incorporating a balanced diet, regular exercise, and stress management can help you address the underlying causes and improve your overall quality of life\u{1F4AA}\u{1F3FD}\n\n\u{1F440}Have you noticed any of these lesser-known signs in yourself or someone close? Let\u2019s normalize discussing all aspects of PCOS, not just the most visible ones in the comments section.\u2935\uFE0F\n\n#pcos #pcod #weighloss #weightissues #reproductivehealth #irregularperiods #menstrualcycle #womenshealth #obgyn #dietandexercise #stressmanagement #skincare #acanthosisnigricans #hirsutism #alopecia #guthealth #pcosweightloss #pcosawareness #pcossupport #fyp #instagram #ahmedabad #valsad #womenshealthphysio #mentalhealth #anxietyawareness #pcosfertility #infertility #trending #womenshealthmatters",
    postedAt: "2024-11-12T13:51:49.000Z",
    approxViews: 28,
    instagramPosterUrl:
      "https://scontent-dfw5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/653936460_18090303863757045_3495788408984525760_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_tt6&_nc_cat=107&ig_cache_key=MzQ5OTcyMjk1MTI1MzM3NDgzMQ%3D%3D.3-ccb7-5&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=58cdad&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6IkNBUk9VU0VMX0lURU0ueHBpZHMuMTA4MC5zZHIucmVndWxhcl9waG90by5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=kuNJbNoK9iEQ7kNvwEGxoGF&_nc_oc=AdqlLKY9O8Z5txyGQqXff1InqgBpQqmbJeAq9FwLIxHeTLsSGpt1MeIQhJSgNgRnpRo&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=rTDV5mQlYbX9l54ci5M2Dg&_nc_ss=72289&oh=00_AQBiLzMmsws-BO1Bl7NmMbq8lj2muZGRvqwiXYROrLHbCQ&oe=6A5834F9",
