    topics: ["Pilates", "Labor & delivery", "Pelvic floor", "Pregnancy", "Exercise"],
    title:
      "Many women suffer in silence, oblivious to how physiotherapy can aid in the prevention, treatment, and recovery of a \u2026",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "Many women suffer in silence, oblivious to how physiotherapy can aid in the prevention, treatment, and recovery of a wide range of women's health issues.\nThe following are some of the conditions for which you should see a women's health physiotherapist.\n\n1) MENSTRUAL DISORDERS - Disorders like Pre Menstrual Syndrome & Dysmenorrhea and hormonal problems like PCOS & Endometriosis can be managed by doing exercises when correctly prescribed. It helps to improve your mood, regularise periods and reduces menstrual cramps.\n\n2) FEMALE ATHLETE - Female athletes differ from their male counterparts in that they require a tailored approach to exercise as well as injury treatment and prevention.\n\n3) PRE/POST NATAL PHYSIOTHERAPY - A proper Physiotherapy programme can manage pregnancy issues like back pain, stress incontinence, or other musculoskeletal dysfunctions, and  postnatal issues like Diastasis (separation of abdominal muscles) or decreased strength of pelvic floor. It also helps you prepare for childbirth.\n\n4) PELVIC FLOOR DYSFUNCTION - A hypotone or hypertone pelvic floor can cause urinary/fecal incontinence, uterine prolapse, or sexual problems. Depending on the cause and symptoms, a WHP can prescribe exercises to treat the patient.\n\n5) POST ABDOMINAL/GYNAE SURGERY - Exercises can help you regain your functional self after a surgery such as a C-section or a Hysterectomy (removal of uterus).\n\n6) MENOPAUSAL SYMPTOMS - Exercise has been shown to be effective in treating menopausal symptoms such as stress, weight gain, and decreased bone mass density.\n\n7) LYMPHEDEMA - Post-gynecologic or breast cancer surgery Lymphedema is one of the complications that can be treated with exercises.\n\n8) CLINICAL PILATES - It improves deep abdominal and pelvic floor muscle tone, posture, overall muscle tone, and is a safe form of exercise during and after pregnancy.",
