    doctor: "zalak",
    topics: ["Pelvic floor", "Pregnancy", "Patient education", "Posts"],
    title: "\u201CWhy is my baby moving less today?\u201D \u{1F630}",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u201CWhy is my baby moving less today?\u201D \u{1F630}\n\nIf you\u2019ve ever typed this into Google, you\u2019re not alone.\n\nA change in your baby\u2019s movements can be worrying but not every quieter moment means something is wrong. Knowing what\u2019s normal for your baby is what really matters.\n\nHere\u2019s something many moms don\u2019t know \u{1F447}\u{1F3FD} \n\n\u{1F90D} Babies have sleep cycles in the womb, so it\u2019s normal for them to have quiet periods. But if your baby\u2019s movements are noticeably different from their usual pattern, don\u2019t ignore it.\n\n\u{1F90D} Did you know babies can even respond to sounds and familiar voices before birth? \nOver time, you\u2019ll begin to recognize your baby\u2019s own unique rhythm and activity pattern.\n\nThe key isn\u2019t comparing your pregnancy with someone else\u2019s.. it\u2019s getting to know your baby\u2019s normal.\n\nSwipe through this carousel to learn:\n\u2728 When you\u2019ll usually start feeling movements\n\u2728 Why some moms feel kicks later than others\n\u2728 Common myths about baby movements\n\u2728 When it\u2019s time to contact your healthcare provider\n\n\u{1F4BE} Save this post for your pregnancy journey.. you may need it when questions pop into your mind.\n\u{1F4E4} Share it with an expecting mom because this is information every pregnant woman deserves to know.\n\u{1F4AC} Tell us in the comments: When did you first feel your baby\u2019s movements?\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ Baby movements, fetal movements, baby kicks, reduced baby movements, baby not moving, baby moving less, fetal kick count, kick count, baby kick count, pregnancy, pregnancy care, pregnancy tips, pregnancy symptoms, healthy pregnancy, pregnancy education, pregnancy advice, pregnancy journey, prenatal care, antenatal care, second trimester, third trimester, expecting mom, first-time mom, baby movement in pregnancy, when to worry about baby movements, anterior placenta, pregnancy myths, pregnancy safety, fetal wellbeing, baby activity in womb, pregnancy health, gynecologist, women\u2019s health, pelvic floor physiotherapy, pregnancy physiotherapy, maternity care, pregnancy support, pregnancy awareness, pregnancy India, mom to be, expecting parents ]\n#babykicks #babymovement #pregnancy #firsttimemom #fyp",
    instagramPosterUrl:
      "https://scontent-sjc3-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/746528243_18021417323904586_2519630267791612726_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_p640x640_sh2.08_tt6&_nc_ht=scontent-sjc3-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_cat=110&_nc_oc=Q6cZ2gFzEEOEJWuZirwRrYcq0TWjY1l6WM9TEI23rNuvOnZ2eD3L6KkEIYEYTsul9kRRrtU&_nc_ohc=96FEWNdpTwQQ7kNvwHlKMpF&_nc_gid=YsqwexhNmclG9W-SVmckHg&edm=ALY_pVYBAAAA&ccb=7-5&oh=00_AQC_DAxGPzyzD_FcsRJhIeQxJXxd_QxECIF7-dyrXm5bhQ&oe=6A5E8FC8&_nc_sid=57e406",
