    title: "Women's Health Duo ,  Instagram Reel",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u201CWhich contraception is best for us?\u201D \u{1F914}\n\nOne of the most common questions couples ask and the answer is: it depends.\n\nFrom condoms, birth control pills, Copper-T, hormonal IUCDs, injections, implants, emergency contraception, to permanent methods for men and women, there are many options available today.\n\n\u2728 Each method has its own benefits, effectiveness, side effects, and suitability based on factors like:\n\u2022 Age\n\u2022 Medical history\n\u2022 Future pregnancy plans\n\u2022 Breastfeeding status\n\u2022 Lifestyle and personal preferences\n\nThat\u2019s why choosing contraception should never be based solely on what worked for a friend, family member, or something you saw online.\n\nThe right contraceptive is the one that fits your health, your goals, and your relationship.\n\n\u{1F4AC} If you and your partner are currently considering contraception, what is your biggest concern\u2026 effectiveness, side effects, hormones, or future fertility?\n\n\u{1F447}\u{1F3FD} Comment below and let\u2019s discuss.\n\n\u{1F4CC} Save this reel for future reference and share it with your partner before making a decision.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ contraception, family planning, couple, cafeteria approach of contraception, male and female contraception options, fertility, pregnancy, pros and cons of contraception, what type of contraception is better for whom, explore page, women\u2019s health ]\n#contraception #womenshealth #pregnancy #familyplanning #fyp",
