    title: "Women's Health Duo ,  Instagram Reel",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "Before it became what we know as Pilates today, it was called \u201CContrology\u201D a method created by Joseph Pilates.\n\nHis journey shaped the method.\nAs a child, he struggled with multiple health issues, which led him to deeply study the body, movement, and strength. During World War I, he worked with injured soldiers, using spring-based resistance to help them recover.. laying the foundation for what we now know as Pilates equipment.\n\nWhen he later opened his studio in New York, Contrology became a space for healing, strength, and movement, especially among dancers and performers.\n\nContrology wasn\u2019t just exercise.\nIt was a system of movement built on:\n\n\u2022 breath\n\u2022 control\n\u2022 precision\n\u2022 flow\n\u2022 centering (the powerhouse)\n\u2022 alignment\n\nEvery movement had intention.\nEvery transition had purpose.\n\nHe believed:\n\u201CIt is the mind itself which builds the body.\u201D\n\nOver the years, Pilates has evolved & that evolution is important too.\n\nToday, we understand more about biomechanics, rehabilitation, pelvic health, and the nervous system. This allows us to adapt the method for modern bodies.. making it more accessible, therapeutic, and relevant.\n\nWe modify. We personalise. We meet the body where it is. But the essence remains.\n\nAt its core, Pilates still teaches you how to move.\nHow to find your neutral spine,\nengage your deep core,\nmove with control over momentum,\nand connect breath with movement.\n\nAnd that\u2019s why I LOVEEEEE Pilates \u{1F60D}\n\nBecause it goes beyond a workout.\nIt builds awareness that stays with you.. in how you move, sit, stand & live.\n\nSimple, but never easy. Subtle, but deeply powerful.\n\nOn World Pilates Day, this is just a reminder of where it all began & why it still matters \u{1F90D}\n\nIf you truly love Pilates, read\n\u{1F4D6} Return to Life Through Contrology\n.\n.\n[ International Pilates Day, Pilates Instructor, Women\u2019s Health Physiotherapist, STOTT Pilates Instructor, Joseph Pilates Method, Contrology, Principles of Pilates, Mat Pilates, Classical Mat Pilates, Joseph Pilates teaching video, Contemporary Pilates, Reformer, Pelvic Health, Gynecologist, Pilates Day 2026 ] \n#pilatesday #josephpilatesmethod #matpilates #classicalpilates #stottpilates",
