    instagramCaption:
      "You don\u2019t need every supplement in pregnancy.\nYou need the right ones \u{1F48A}\u2728\n\nMost women are told what to take\u2026\nbut not what is actually essential vs optional \u{1F447}\u{1F3FD} \n\n\u{1F338} Must-have (usually prescribed as supplements)\nThese are difficult to meet through diet alone and are almost always needed:\n\n\u2022 Folic Acid \u2013 critical for baby\u2019s brain & spine (especially early pregnancy)\n\u2022 Iron \u2013 prevents anemia and supports increased blood demand\n\u2022 Calcium + Vitamin D \u2013 baby\u2019s bones + maternal bone protection\n\u2022 Vitamin B12 \u2013 baby\u2019s brain & nerve development (very important in vegetarians)\n\n\u2728 Can be managed through diet (supplement if needed)\n\n\u2022 Protein \u2013 from dal, dairy, eggs, nuts\n\u2022 Omega-3 (DHA) \u2013 from walnuts, seeds (supplements if intake is low)\n\n\u2696\uFE0F Only if required (based on symptoms/reports)\n\n\u2022 Magnesium \u2013 for cramps, sleep issues\n\u2022 Zinc \u2013 if deficiency or low immunity\n\u2022 Iodine \u2013 usually covered through iodized salt/prenatal vitamins\n\n\u{1F6AB} What you should NOT do:\nDon\u2019t take multiple supplements randomly\nDon\u2019t copy someone else\u2019s prescription\nDon\u2019t assume \u201Cmore is better\u201D\n\n\u{1F4A1} The right way:\nThese are the nutrients your body needs, \nbut your dosage and supplements should be personalised\n\n\u26A0\uFE0F Always consult your doctor before starting any supplement\n\n\u{1F90D} Save this.. you\u2019ll need it later \u2665\uFE0F\n\u{1F90D} Share this with a pregnant woman who deserves the right guidance \u{1F930}\u{1F3FB}\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ pregnancy, pregnancy supplements, recommended dose, supplements during pregnancy and its importance, pregnant, moms to be, relatable to first time moms, diet and nutrition in pregnancy, folic acid, iron, calcium, vitamin d, vitamin b 12, omega 3, choline, zinc, magnesium, baby\u2019s brain development, protein in pregnancy, baby\u2019s growth, pregnancy diet, exercise in pregnancy, obstetrician & gynaecologist, women\u2019s health physiotherapist, second trimester, third trimester, relatable pregnancy, explore page, share this with moms to be, indian pregnant woman, neural tube defects ]\n#supplements #pregnancy #dose #importance #fyp",
