    title: "Women's Health Duo ,  Instagram Reel",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "If you are pregnant and have ever thought..\n\u201CWhat if I can\u2019t handle labor pain?\nWhat if it gets too intense?\nWhat if I panic in that moment?\nHow will I even know what to do?\u201D\n\nYou\u2019re not alone. Almost every mom has these thoughts at some point.\n\nAnd honestly, that\u2019s because no one really explains how to use information during labor.\n\nThis is exactly where a labor & delivery session helps:\n\n\u{1F538} You understand what labor actually feels like and how it progresses, so you\u2019re not second guessing every pain\n\u{1F538} You learn when to go to the hospital, instead of going too early or rushing in panic\n\u{1F538} You\u2019re taught how to breathe and move during contractions, not just theoretically\n\u{1F538} You practice positions that can actually make labor smoother and more comfortable\n\u{1F538} You understand how to push, and more importantly, how to relax your pelvic floor at the right time\n\u{1F538} Your partner also knows how to support you, instead of feeling lost\n\nIt doesn\u2019t make labor \u201Ceasy\u201D \nbut it makes you feel much more in control of what\u2019s happening.\n\nAnd that changes the whole experience.\n\nBecause when you understand your body and trust the process,\nthings feel less overwhelming\u2026 and a lot more manageable \u{1F90D}\n\n\u{1F6A8} Most moms realise this only after delivery, don\u2019t be one of them!\n\n\u{1F449}\u{1F3FC} Save & share this with a mom-to-be who needs to feel more prepared for her labor \u{1F930}\u{1F3FB}\n.\n.\n.\n\n.\n[ Labor and delivery session, partner support during childbirth, labor pain, labor and its stages, how to push during labor, pelvic floor contraction and relaxation, strategies to cope with labor pain, true and false labor, true signs of labor, vaginal delivery, normal delivery, women\u2019s health physiotherapist, childbirth, obstetrician and gynaecologist, labor pain fear, c section, prenatal exercises, prenatal pilates, third trimester workout, education on labor and childbirth, things to know, things every pregnant woman should know, labor preparation, awareness, labor prep exercises, pushing techniques, breathing exercises during labor, fyp ]\n#laboranddelivery #pregnant #laborpains #tips #education",
