    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "Being a Physiotherapist & Pilates instructor has taught me one thing again and again..\nyou can\u2019t pour from an empty cup \u{1F64C}\u{1F3FD}\n\nEvery day I help women move better, feel stronger, and take care of their bodies\u2026\nand this journey constantly reminds me to do the same for myself \u{1F9D8}\u{1F3FB}\u200D\u2640\uFE0F\n\nMovement isn\u2019t just about workouts\nIt\u2019s about:\n\u2022 supporting your hormones\n\u2022 building strength for every phase of life\n\u2022 preventing pain before it starts\n\u2022 feeling energised in your own body\n\nAnd for women, this matters even more\nbecause our bodies go through so many changes, \nwhether you have PCOS, are pregnant, or are in the perimenopause phase \u{1F342}\n\nStaying active is not a luxury, it\u2019s a necessity \u{1F4AF} \n\nStart with 10 minutes. Start small. Just start \u2728\n\nSAVE this for the days you feel low on motivation\n& SHARE this with a woman who always puts herself last \u{1FA77}\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ movement, pilates, womens health, womens health physiotherapist, gynecologist, hormonal health, staying active, motivation, mat pilates, pilates instructor, STOTT pilates instructor, women empowerment, movement is medicine, reformer pilates, women in healthcare, healthcare professionals, physical therapist, pelvic health, physiotherapist, pilates girlie, in my pilates era, posture, strong core, movement principles, strong girls ]\n#pilates #womenshealth #hormonalhealth #doctor #fyp",
