    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "Most pregnancy advice falls into two extremes \u274C\nOver-resting or random, unguided workouts!\u{1F644}\n\nAnd that\u2019s exactly where most moms get stuck \u{1F605}\n\nDuring pregnancy, the biggest mistakes I see are -\n\n\u2022 ignoring pain thinking \u201Cthis is normal\u201D\n\u2022 doing absolutely nothing because \u201Cbetter safe than sorry\u201D\n\u2022 or following random workouts/advice without knowing if it\u2019s right for your body\n\nHere\u2019s the truth \u{1F913}\n\n\u{1F538} Every pregnancy is different\n\u{1F538} What\u2019s safe for one mom may not be right for another\n\u{1F538} Pain is information, not something to \u201Cpush through\u201D\n\u{1F538} Movement is important.. but the right kind, at the right time\n\nIt\u2019s not about doing everything.\nIt\u2019s about doing what\u2019s right for YOU \u2728\n\n\u{1F4AC} Comment \u201CGUIDE\u201D if you\u2019re confused about what to do in your trimester\n\u{1F930} Save this if you\u2019re pregnant or send it to a mama who needs this reminder\n\n[ pregnancy myths, exercise during pregnancy, guidance during pregnancy, pregnancy workout, prenatal pilates, pregnancy mistakes, prenatal fitness, pregnancy tips for moms, dos and donts during pregnancy, pain during pregnancy, pregnancy physiotherapy, women\u2019s health physiotherapist, indian moms, prenatal classes in india, online prenatal class, pregnancy care india, first time moms ]\n\n#pregnancyfitness #prenatal #pilates #physioterapy #pregnancymyths",
