    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u{1F4AD} \u201CJust do Kegels every day.. it\u2019ll make labor easier!\u201D\nSound familiar? \u{1F64B}\u{1F3FB}\u200D\u2640\uFE0F You\u2019re definitely not alone.\n\n\u{1F440} But here\u2019s what most people don\u2019t explain:\nYour pelvic floor isn\u2019t just about squeezing stronger. It also needs to relax, lengthen, and let go during birth.\n\n\u27A1\uFE0F For some, pelvic floor strengthening is helpful - yes, Kegels can improve support and prevent leaks.\n\u27A1\uFE0F But many pregnant women have pelvic floors that are tight or overactive\u2026 and doing more Kegels can actually make relaxing harder when it matters most \u{1F62E}\u200D\u{1F4A8}\n\n\u2728 What really prepares you for birth is pelvic floor awareness, knowing when to contract and when to fully release.\nBecause during delivery, strength alone won\u2019t cut it. Being able to let go is just as important.\n\n\u{1F469}\u{1F3FB}\u200D\u2695\uFE0F As a pelvic health physio, I assess your individual pelvic floor needs and guide you through exercises that help your body get ready for labor the right way.. no unnecessary squeezing or guessing.\n\n\u{1F4E9} DM us \u201CBIRTH\u201D to find out more about our labor prep sessions (spoiler: it\u2019s not just about Kegels \u{1F609})\n\n\u{1F447}\u{1F3FD} Have you been told to do Kegels for birth? Share your story or tag a mama who needs to hear this! \n\n#fyp #womenshealth #obgyn #ahmedabad #pregnancy #pregnant #womenshealthphysio #instagood #gynecologist #obstetrician #pelvicfloor #pelvichealth #pelvicfloorexercises #pelvicfloorphysicaltherapy #pelvicfloorhealth #childbirth #labor #laboranddelivery #vaginaldelivery #childbirtheducation #laborprep #physio #physicaltherapist #trend #pelvic #kegel #kegels #kegelexercises #gynecphysiotherapy #india",
