      "\u201CIt\u2019s just period pain\u201D - or is it? \u{1F914}\u{1F4AD}\n\nSevere period cramps that disrupt your daily routine aren\u2019t normal! If you find yourself curled up in pain every month, missing work, or popping painkillers like candy\u{1F36C} - it\u2019s time to dig deeper.\n\nOne possible culprit? Endometriosis. \nThis condition occurs when endometrial-like tissue grows outside the uterus, leading to chronic pelvic pain, painful periods (dysmenorrhea), pain during intercourse (dyspareunia), and even infertility. \n\nSounds serious? That\u2019s because it is! Yet, so many suffer in silence because period pain is often dismissed as \u201Cjust part of being a woman.\u201D\n\n\u{1F6A8} Newsflash: Debilitating pain is NOT normal! \u{1F6A8}\n\nIf your period pain feels like it\u2019s taking over your life, don\u2019t brush it off - book an appointment with your gynecologist and get checked for conditions like endometriosis. Early diagnosis can make all the difference!\u2728\n\n#womenshealth #ahmedabad #fyp #obgyn #instagood #gynecologist #womenshealthphysio #endometriosis #endo #endowarrior #endometriosisawarenessmonth #period #periodpain #cramp #periodcramps #womenshealthduo #infertility #awareness #endometriosisawareness #endopain #menstrualcycle #womenshealthmatters #valsad #india #obstetriciangynecologist #womenshealthcare #healthawareness",
