    instagramCaption:
      "AMH - a tiny hormone with a big impact on your fertility!\u{1F95A}\u{1F4A1} \nIt\u2019s produced by small follicles in your ovaries and gives an estimate of your ovarian reserve (aka how many eggs you\u2019ve got left).\n\n\u{1F449}\u{1F3FC}Here\u2019s something you might not know: AMH doesn\u2019t just guide fertility planning, it also helps diagnose conditions like PCOS or low ovarian reserve. \u{1FA7A} \nAnd for Indian women, AMH levels can start to decline earlier, sometimes even in their late 20s or early 30s!\n\n\u{1F9D0}Thinking of delaying pregnancy, exploring egg freezing, or just curious? Checking your AMH can help you make informed decisions. \n\u203C\uFE0FBut remember, AMH is just one piece of the puzzle, other factors like egg quality and overall health matter too!\n\n\u{1F506}Ready to plan smarter? Let\u2019s talk in the comments!\u{1F447}\u{1F3FD}\n\n#antimullarianhormone #amh #fertility #infertility #pco #womenshealth #pregnancy #eggfreezing #eggs #ovaries #uterus #female #reproductivehealth #health #healthandwellness #pregnancyplanning #fertilityplan #hormones #test #fyp #ahmedabad #valsad #obstetrician #gynecologist #womenshealthphysio #instagood #pregnant_world #tips #family #familyplanning",
