    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u{1F930}\u{1F3FB}Paracetamol During Pregnancy: Safe Choice or Extra Caution?\u{1F914}\n\n\u{1F538}In every Indian home, Dolo 650 is the go-to for fever and pain relief. But when you\u2019re pregnant, even everyday meds require extra care. \n\u{1F9D0}So, is it safe to reach for paracetamol during pregnancy? Here\u2019s what you need to know.\u{1F476}\u{1F3FB}\u2728\n\n\u25B6\uFE0FFirst Trimester: In these early months when your baby\u2019s development is delicate, stick to the lowest effective dose (325-500 mg) and use it only for occasional relief. Always consult your gynecologist first! \u{1FA7A}\n\n\u25B6\uFE0FSecond & Third Trimesters: Later in pregnancy, doses up to 650 mg are generally safe as needed, but don\u2019t exceed 4g per day. Even then, short-term use is key to minimizing risks.\u{1F48A}\n\n\u203C\uFE0FReminder: Always check with your gynecologist before taking any medication in pregnancy. Even common meds like paracetamol need professional guidance to protect you and your baby.\u{1F338}\n\nHave questions about other meds during pregnancy? Drop them in the comments, let\u2019s chat!\u2B07\uFE0F\n\n#pregnancy #pregnant #pregnancymedicine #medical #medication #dosage #dose #paracetamol #dolo #dolo650 #obgyn #obstetrician #valsad #ahmedabad #instagood #fyp #instagram #healthypregnancy #healthylifestyle #healthcare #healthcareprofessional #pregnant_world #pregnantbelly #pregnancydiary #womenshealth #pregnancylife #baby #trimester #fetus #healthtips",
