    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "Did You Know These Fascinating Facts About Newborns?\u{1F476}\u{1F3FB}\u2728\n\n\u{1F970}Newborns may be tiny, but they\u2019re full of incredible surprises that make the first few months so special! \n\u{1F929}From unique reflexes to surprising senses, here are some fun facts about your little one\u2019s amazing abilities:\n\n\u25B6\uFE0FThey See the World in Black, White, and Gray \u{1F5A4}\u{1F90D}: \nFor the first couple of months, newborns can only see high-contrast colors. By 2-3 months, they start recognizing bright colors like red and yellow, which are easier for their developing eyes to process.\n\n\u25B6\uFE0FStronger Than They Look!\u{1F4AA}\u{1F3FD}: \nNewborns may seem delicate, but they\u2019re surprisingly strong. Check out their grasp reflex, it allows them to hold your finger tightly, an instinct that dates back to survival needs.\n\n\u25B6\uFE0FBuilt-In Reflexes\u270B\u{1F3FC}: \nBabies have amazing reflexes! The Moro reflex (or startle reflex) makes them throw out their arms when startled, and the rooting reflex helps them find a breast or bottle for feeding by turning their head toward touch.\n\n\u{1F913}Did any of these surprise you? Comment below with what you found the most fascinating and let us know if you\u2019d love to see more fun facts! \u2B07\uFE0F\n\n#newborn #babies #baby #fun #funfacts #interestingfacts #reflexes #primitivereflexes #babydevelopment #newbornbaby #pediatrics #peds #obgyn #knowledge #fyp #instagram #trend #womenshealth #pregnant #postdelivery #laboranddelivery #womenshealthphysio #babysofinstagram #babystyle #postpartum #earlypostpartum #india #ahmedabad #valsad",
