    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u203C\uFE0FPregnancy myths: Everyone\u2019s got one, and the internet is FULL of them! But what\u2019s the science behind it all? We\u2019re here to break down the truth vs. the tall tales.\u{1F913}\n\n\u27A1\uFE0FEvery pregnancy is different, which is why one mom may be given unique advice that doesn\u2019t apply to another. \n\n\u{1F505}For example, while light exercise is generally encouraged, a mom-to-be with a high-risk condition like placenta previa might be advised to rest more. \n\u2755Factors like maternal health, baby\u2019s development, and overall risk make personalized guidance essential.\n\u{1F6A8}Always consult your gynecologist for advice that\u2019s right for you.\n\n\u{1F9D0}Got a myth you\u2019ve heard or a question on your mind? Drop it in the comments - we\u2019re here to set the record straight!\u2935\uFE0F\n\n#mythvsfact #myth #facts #pregnancy #pregnant #obgyn #csection #exercise #thirdtrimester #pregnancymyths #science #womenshealth #consulting #diet #dietandexercise #nutrition #boyorgirl #ultrasound #baby #fyp #instagood #insta #gynecology #obs #pregnantbelly #pregnancylife #pregnancyjourney #pregnancyworkout #pregnancystyle #pregnantstyle",
