    instagramCaption:
      "\u{1FA78}Periods delayed? Not necessarily PCOS!\u{1F6AB} \n\n\u{1F506}Despite PCOS being a common cause, other factors could be at play. \nStress, weight changes, hormonal imbalances, and even travel can impact your cycle.\u{1F30D} \nUnderstanding your body\u2019s signals is key!\u{1F511} \n\n\u{1F4AC} Consult your Gynaecologist for personalised advice and tests to rule out underlying issues.\u{1FA7A} \n\u203C\uFE0FRemember, irregularities happen to many, and tracking symptoms can lead to better health insights. \u{1F4CA}\n\n[ PCOS, Delayed periods, Menstrual cycle, Menstrual irregularities, Delayed menstrual cycle, Period, Hormonal imbalances, Thyroid function, Sleep disturbances, Diet and Exercise, Weight gain, Weight loss, Menses, PCOD, Obstetrician & Gynaecologist, Dr Charmi Shah, Ahmedabad, Valsad, Gujarat, India, Stress & anxiety, Birth control pills, Hormonal changes]",
