    topics: ["Labor & delivery", "Pelvic floor", "Pregnancy", "Exercise", "Reels"],
    title: "Women's Health Duo ,  Instagram Reel",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u2728Post-partum exercise guideline\u2728\n\n\u27A1\uFE0FAfter childbirth, resuming exercise is a crucial step for recovery, but it\u2019s important to approach it correctly. \n\n\u27A1\uFE0FGenerally, most women can start gentle exercises around 4-6 weeks postpartum. However, recovery differs between vaginal deliveries and cesarean sections due to the varying impacts on the body.\n\n\u27A1\uFE0FVaginal deliveries often allow for a quicker return to physical activity, while C-sections, being major surgeries, require a more cautious approach. \n\n\u{1F4CC}Each woman\u2019s body heals at its own pace, and individual strength and circumstances vary widely.\n\n\u203C\uFE0FTo ensure you are exercising safely and effectively, it is essential to get assessed by your gynecologist and a women\u2019s health physiotherapist. They can provide a tailored exercise plan that suits your specific recovery needs, helping you heal and regain strength properly. Remember, personalized care is key to a healthy recovery and optimal postpartum fitness.\u{1F4AA}\u{1F3FD}\n\n\u{1F48C}\u{1F447}\u{1F3FD}Comment down or DM us your queries if you want to know more about post-partum fitness!\u{1F607}\n\n[ Post-partum, Normal delivery vs C-section, Post-partum fitness, obstetrics & Gynaecology, Women\u2019s Health Physiotherapist, Pelvic floor exercises, Strength training, Posture correction, Breastfeeding, Nimaaya Health, Ahmedabad, India ]",
    postedAt: "2024-07-05T14:14:06.000Z",
    approxViews: 5169,
