    instagramCaption:
      "\u{1F9D0}Did you know that STRESS can have a huge impact on your PCOS?\n\u{1F538}After we experience a stressful event, insulin resistance can develop 4-6 hours after which can cause ovulation to delay, androgen excess and increased fat storage.\n\n\u27A1\uFE0FHere are simple ways in managing stress with PCOS - \n\n\u{1F538} Meditation\n\u{1F538}Exercise\n\u{1F538}Sunlight\n\u{1F538}Limiting sugar\n\u{1F538}Communication\n\u{1F538}Including healthy fats and protein in diet\n\u{1F538}Sleep\n\n\u27A1\uFE0FThe best way to care for PCOS involves whole body and mind care and not just hormonal birth control and weight loss. \n\nWhat do you do for managing your stress and PCOS\u2753\nLet us know in the comment section \u2B07\uFE0F",
