    topics: ["Exercise", "Patient education", "Reels"],
    title: "Women's Health Duo ,  Instagram Reel",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "Are you feeling ready to go and start a workout post-partum\u2753\n\n\u{1F538}It is so important to go slow, let your body heal & rest when you feel overworked, overwhelmed or overtired! \n\u{1F538}Jumping right back into high intensity exercise will lead to prolonged healing and more likely to have aches/pain down the road.\n\u{1F538}It should be focused on honoring your body, not about forcing or restricting or overloading it.\n\n\u{1F446}\u{1F3FD}Here are few exercises and tips for re-gaining your core strength and getting back into the swing of things!\n\n\u{1F914}Are you someone who wants to get back to exercising post-partum but don't know when and how?\n\u27A1\uFE0FWe recommend you to see a Women's Health Physiotherapist who can guide you and help you with an individualised exercise program depending on your current status and strength!\n\n\u{1F48C}DM us for more such information and consultation!\u{1F60A}",
