      "The 21st of March is WORLD DOWN SYNDROME DAY!\nThe goal of this day is to raise awareness about Down Syndrome and to reduce the social stigma that patients face. \nIt is a genetic disorder that affects over 30,000 children in India. It occurs when there is unnatural cell division as a result of chromosome 21 replication. India, like every developing country, struggles to provide timely medical aid and education to people diagnosed with Developmental Disorders, particularly those from economically depressed families. \n\n\u2B50Did you know that prenatal testing allows you and your family to identify Down syndrome as early as 11 weeks of pregnancy?\n\u27A1\uFE0FPregnant women are offered routine prenatal tests at various stages of their pregnancy for a variety of reasons, including: Screening tests (Double marker test, NT Scan, NIPT, etc.) that determine the likelihood of having a baby with a genetic condition.\n\nYour healthcare provider is the best person to ask if you have any questions or concerns!\n\u{1F48C} DM us for more!",
