    topics: ["Fertility", "Pregnancy", "Exercise", "Reels"],
    title: "Women's Health Duo ,  Instagram Reel",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "While you've probably heard about the various appointments you'll need during your pregnancy, there's one that comes before you even try to conceive: The PRE-CONCEPTION Appointment.\n\nWe believe that scheduling a pre-conception appointment is an excellent way to ensure the healthiest pregnancy possible.\nIt is a visit with your OBGYN during which you can get all of your questions about fertility, getting pregnant, the early stages of pregnancy, and anything else you need to know based on your medical history answered.\n\nHere's a quick rundown of what you might talk about:\n\n\u27A1\uFE0FYour plans for children and when to stop taking birth control\n\u27A1\uFE0FYour medical, surgical, and family history of diseases\n\u27A1\uFE0FChanges in lifestyle or adjustments\n\u27A1\uFE0FHow your body fat percentage may influence conception?\n\u27A1\uFE0FTests and vaccinations\n\u27A1\uFE0FWhen should you start taking prenatal vitamins, and which ones should you take?\n\u27A1\uFE0FHow to begin actually trying to Conceive?\n\u27A1\uFE0F Exercise and Nutrition \n\nOur advice - Make the most of your time by understanding what steps to take to ensure a healthy pregnancy and baby!\u{1F60A}\n\n\u{1F48C}DM us for consultation!",
