    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "If Netflix actually made this documentary, it wouldn\u2019t fit into one season.\n\nBecause postpartum recovery is still treated like the part of childbirth that somehow takes care of itself.\n\nYou\u2019ve probably Googled at least one of these:\n\n\u{1F538}Why does my lower back still hurt postpartum?\n\u{1F538}Why do I still look pregnant months after giving birth?\n\u{1F538}What is diastasis recti?\n\u{1F538}When can I safely start exercising after a normal delivery or C-section?\n\u{1F538}Is pain during sex after childbirth normal?\n\u{1F538}Why does my C-section scar still feel tight or numb?\n\u{1F538}Why does my pelvis feel heavy when I stand?\n\nAnd somewhere along the way, many moms hear:\n\u2728 \u201CGive it time.\u201D\n\u2728 \u201CThat\u2019s just part of motherhood.\u201D\n\u2728 \u201CYour body will figure it out.\u201D\nIf only healing worked on motivational quotes \u{1F642}\n\nThe truth is, recovery after childbirth is more than waiting.\n\nYour pelvic floor, abdominal muscles (diastasis recti), breathing mechanics, C-section or perineal scar, posture, core strength, and return to daily activities and exercise all deserve proper assessment and rehabilitation.. not assumptions.\n\nPostpartum rehabilitation isn\u2019t about getting your \u201Cpre-baby body\u201D back.\n\nIt\u2019s about helping you:\n\u2714\uFE0F Move without pain.\n\u2714\uFE0F Laugh or sneeze without leaking urine.\n\u2714\uFE0F Lift your baby confidently.\n\u2714\uFE0F Return to exercise safely.\n\u2714\uFE0F Reduce pelvic heaviness and pressure.\n\u2714\uFE0F Rebuild strength instead of guessing your way through recovery.\n\nMotherhood shouldn\u2019t automatically come with discomfort that you\u2019re expected to silently accept.\n\nIf you\u2019ve ever been told \u201Cit\u2019s normal after childbirth,\u201D ask a better question:\n\nIs it common or is it actually something that can be treated?\n\nBecause those aren\u2019t always the same thing.\n\n\u{1F4AC} Tell me in the comments: What\u2019s one postpartum symptom nobody warned you about?\n\n\u{1F90D} Send it to a new mom who deserves to know that recovery is something she deserves\u2026 not something she simply has to \u201Cget through.\u201D\n.\n[ post partum moms, post partum rehab, diastasis recti, post C section recovery, back pain post delivery, urine leakage while laughing ]\n#postpartum #rehab #netflixdocumentary #pelvicfloorphysicaltherapy #fyp",
