    topics: ["Exercise", "Patient education", "Reels"],
    title: "\u{1F6A8} Pubic pain while getting out of bed during pregnancy?\u{1F930}\u{1F3FB}",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "\u{1F6A8} Pubic pain while getting out of bed during pregnancy?\u{1F930}\u{1F3FB} \n\nThat sharp pain at the front of your pelvis isn\u2019t \u201Cjust part of pregnancy.\u201D\n\nDuring pregnancy, hormones such as relaxin help prepare your body for birth by increasing ligament laxity. As your baby grows, the load on your pelvis also increases. Together, these changes can make the pubic symphysis (the joint at the front of your pelvis) more sensitive and less stable, especially during movements where one leg moves independently.\n\nThat\u2019s why getting out of bed the wrong way can make it worse.\n\n\u274C Avoid:\n\u2022 Twisting your pelvis\n\u2022 Moving one leg at a time\n\u2022 Letting your knees separate\n\u2022 Sitting up by twisting\n\n\u2705 Instead:\n\u2022 Keep your knees together\n\u2022 Log roll onto your side\n\u2022 Move your shoulders and hips together\n\u2022 Use your arms to push yourself up\n\u2022 Bring both legs off the bed together\n\nThe goal is to reduce shearing forces across the pubic symphysis and keep your pelvis moving as one unit.\n\n\u2728 I\u2019ll be sharing more practical tips and exercises to help you manage pregnancy pelvic pain and make everyday movements more comfortable.\n\n\u{1F4AC} Comment \u201CEXERCISE\u201D and I\u2019ll share more exercises and tips to help manage this pain.\n\n\u{1F4CC} Save this Reel and share it with an expecting mama who needs this.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ Pubic pain during pregnancy, Pregnancy pelvic pain, Pelvic girdle pain (PGP), Pubic symphysis pain, Getting out of bed during pregnancy, Pain turning in bed during pregnancy, Pregnancy physiotherapy, Pregnancy exercise, Pregnancy tips, SPD pregnancy, Sharp pain in front of your pelvis, Women\u2019s Health Physiotherapy, How to get out of bed during pregnancy ] \n#pubicpain #pregnancy #tips #fyp #womenshealth",
