    title:
      "Pubic pain during pregnancy? It might be your pubic symphysis & not \u201Cjust a normal part of pregnancy.\u201D\u{1F930}\u{1F3FB}",
    summary: "Patient education from @womenshealthduo on Instagram.",
    instagramCaption:
      "Pubic pain during pregnancy? It might be your pubic symphysis & not \u201Cjust a normal part of pregnancy.\u201D\u{1F930}\u{1F3FB} \n\nIf turning in bed, getting out of the car, climbing stairs, standing on one leg, or even walking has become painful, you could be experiencing Pregnancy-Related Pelvic Girdle Pain (PGP) or Symphysis Pubis Dysfunction (SPD).\n\nDuring pregnancy, hormonal changes increase ligament laxity while your growing baby changes your body\u2019s centre of gravity and the way forces are transferred through the pelvis. When the muscles that support the pelvis aren\u2019t working together efficiently, the pubic symphysis can become irritated and painful.\n\nThe good news? The right exercises can help.\n\nTargeted strengthening of your glutes, deep core, hip stabilisers, pelvic floor, and inner thigh muscles can improve pelvic stability, reduce excessive stress across the pubic symphysis, and help you move with less pain and more confidence.\n\nPain during pregnancy is common but that doesn\u2019t mean you have to simply put up with it.\n\n\u{1F4CC} Save this reel for when you need it, and share it with a pregnant mama who might be struggling with pubic pain.\n\n\u26A0\uFE0F Disclaimer: Every pregnancy is different. These exercises may not be suitable for everyone. If you have persistent or severe pelvic pain, get assessed by a Women\u2019s Health Physiotherapist and consult your Obstetrician/Gynecologist for an individualized treatment plan.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n.\n[ Pubic symphysis pain pregnancy, Pelvic girdle pain pregnancy, Pubic bone pain pregnancy, Pregnancy pelvic pain, Symphysis Pubis Dysfunction (SPD), SPD pregnancy exercises, Pubic pain during pregnancy, Pelvic pain pregnancy exercises, Pain when walking during pregnancy, Pain turning in bed during pregnancy ]\n#pubicpain #pregnancy #exercise #prenatal #fyp",
